<Shell title="Ahimanikya and Sashisena at Nimuhi Temple" description="The love story, Odia poem and unresolved history behind Sonepur’s doorless temple, with primary text and sources." active="explore" related={false} shareImage={{src:"/assets/nimuhi/nimuhi-memorial-share-v2.jpg",width:1080,height:1440,alt:"Sashisena memorial, also called Nimuhi Mandir, in Sonepur: the pink doorless monument beneath trees. Photograph supplied by Ahimanikya Satapathy."}}>
<article class="nimuhi-story"><p class="eyebrow">Sonepur · Literature and living memory</p><Content/>
<section class="source-scans" aria-labelledby="source-scans-title">
  <p class="eyebrow">Read the source texts</p>
  <h2 id="source-scans-title">From our reading archive</h2>
  <p>These complete scans of printed books are preserved here so you can read the passages for yourself. They are not handwritten manuscripts; the museum manuscript identified in our research is still being sought.</p>
  <div class="source-scan">
    <h3>Shashisena · Prachi Samiti edition</h3>
    <p><a class="scan-link" href="/archive/sashi-sena-prachi-samiti.pdf#page=45">Read the naming passage in the archived PDF</a><span class="scan-size">144 pages · 3.23 MB</span></p>
    <p class="scan-credit">By Pratapa Raya. Scan credited to <a href="http://oaob.nitrkl.ac.in/595/">OaOb</a> and WikiProject Pothi; uploaded to <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sashi_Sena.pdf">Wikimedia Commons</a> by Prateek Pattanaik. Commons identifies the work as <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Template:PD-India">public domain in India</a>. Archived without changes.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="source-scan">
    <h3>Kathalahari · Sixth edition, 1927</h3>
    <p><a class="scan-link" href="/archive/kathalahari-sixth-edition-1927.pdf#page=68">Read the Halahal Kumar story in the archived PDF</a><span class="scan-size">132 pages · 2.60 MB</span></p>
    <p class="scan-credit">Published by Raghabananda Das. Scan from <a href="http://odiabibhaba.in/ପାଠାଗାର/ବହି/">Odia Bibhaba</a>, uploaded to <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kathalahari_(RN_Das,_1927)_opt.pdf">Wikimedia Commons</a> by Jnanaranjan sahu. The scan is listed under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>. Archived without changes.</p>
  </div>
</section>
</article>
</Shell>
